-- title:
--   Ogg's unit at a crossing: tt' = p¹² in the stalk
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \geq 1$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^{2} \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \leq (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit whose image under reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is $1$ (with $M/p$ nonzero in $\mathbb{N}$); assume the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the numerator series of $j$ lies in the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios for $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `XHDRModelAtP` for $X_H(M)$ over $R_p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho \colon R_p \to A$ a ring map compatible with $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O \colon R_p \to O$, with maximal ideal of $O$ generated by $p$, and $O \to \kappa_A$ a ring map with $\mathrm{toκ} \circ \rho_O$ equal to the residue map composed with $\rho$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two components $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$, $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,1$ of the geometric special fibre, and let $x_n$ be its image in $X_O = X_H(M) \times_{R_p} \operatorname{Spec} O$; assume both generic points $\xi_{\infty}$ and $\xi_{0}$ specialise to $x_n$. Then there are germs $t, t'$ in the stalk of $X_O$ at $x_n$ with $t t' = \varpi^{12}$, where $\varpi$ is the germ at $x_n$ of the global function on $X_O$ coming from $p \in O$, with $t$ in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and such that the image of $t$ under the specialisation map to the stalk at $\xi_{\infty}$, or its image in the stalk at $\xi_{0}$, is a unit.
--
--   This is the local form at a crossing of the special fibre of Ogg's modular unit $u = \Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{p})$ and its partner $p^{12}u^{-1}$, whose product is $p^{12}$ and each of which vanishes on exactly one of the two components of the Deligne–Rapoport fibre of $X_H(M)$ at $p$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart) to produce oriented étale coordinates at the crossings, i.e. the local description of $X_H(M)$ over $O$ as $tt' = p^{12}$.
